      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1hhxfxn'
    '|a||So any tax Jon can change, he can dodge. And a tax he can''t change needs facts that only Jon knows.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:zr0trm'
    '|b||James Mirrlees made exactly that the starting point of tax theory, in 1971: the state sees income, never ability. It earned him a share of the 1996 Nobel prize.':
      mp3: 
