      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ro5az9'
    '|b||Greg Mankiw and Matthew Weinzierl ran the standard theory on it: a tall person earning fifty thousand dollars should pay about four and a half thousand more than a short one.':
      mp3: 
